{"name":"Bleeding Crimson","hex":"#9b1414","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bleeding","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of bleed"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Losing blood.","extreme, outright; bloody, blasted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bleeding"},{"term":"crimson","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep, slightly bluish red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a deep red colour.","Immodest. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crimson"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bleeding","blocks":[{"text":"Bleeding, hemorrhage, haemorrhage or blood loss, is blood escaping from the circulatory system from damaged blood vessels. Bleeding can occur internally, or externally either through a natural opening such as the mouth, nose, ear, urethra, genitalia or anus, or through a puncture in the skin.\nHypovolemia is a massive decrease in blood volume, and death by excessive loss of blood is referred to as exsanguination. Typically, a healthy person can endure a loss of 10–15% of the total blood volume without serious medical difficulties. The stopping or controlling of bleeding is called hemostasis and is an important part of both first aid and surgery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Bleeding_finger.jpg/330px-Bleeding_finger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bleeding","wikidata":"Q166019"},{"title":"Crimson","blocks":[{"text":"Crimson is a rich, deep red color, inclining to purple. It originally meant the color of the kermes dye produced from a scale insect, Kermes vermilio, but the name is now sometimes also used as a generic term for slightly bluish-red colors that are between red and rose. It is the national color of Nepal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg/330px-Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson","wikidata":"Q303826"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/A_skateborder_falls_off_his_board_and_cuts_his_hand.jpg/500px-A_skateborder_falls_off_his_board_and_cuts_his_hand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/A_skateborder_falls_off_his_board_and_cuts_his_hand.jpg/1280px-A_skateborder_falls_off_his_board_and_cuts_his_hand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/A_skateborder_falls_off_his_board_and_cuts_his_hand.jpg/500px-A_skateborder_falls_off_his_board_and_cuts_his_hand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bleeding hand wound from a skateboard fall","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_skateborder_falls_off_his_board_and_cuts_his_hand.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Eye_hemorrhage.jpg/500px-Eye_hemorrhage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Eye_hemorrhage.jpg/500px-Eye_hemorrhage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A subconjunctival hemorrhage is a common and relatively minor post-LASIK complication.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEye_hemorrhage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Pulmonary_haemorrhage_-_high_mag.jpg/500px-Pulmonary_haemorrhage_-_high_mag.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Pulmonary_haemorrhage_-_high_mag.jpg/1280px-Pulmonary_haemorrhage_-_